### Truth-law hole caught at the gate (fixed before commit)
- `vein scan --sessions` silently skipped entries that were neither known
  session IDs nor absolute .jsonl paths — unknown ID AND relative path to
  an existing drift fixture both exited 0 with an empty CSV. CORD repro,
  root cause read (resolveRef fall-through swallowed by caller).
- Fix (agnt-vein-resolve-fix via orch-vein): unresolvable entry → stderr
  `UNKNOWN: unresolvable session <token>` + exit 3; relative .jsonl that
  exists resolves honestly (drift fixture → UNKNOWN exit 4). README pins
  the codes. CORD re-verified all three repro cases + full acceptance.

### Usage note (not a defect)
- `latch wait --pane` --until is single-valued (last-wins); CORD's
  `--until done --until idle` watched idle only and timed out at 20m
  despite the pane reaching done. Default (no --until) = idle OR done.
  Documented in README ("match one status").

